NAME
     ps - what is running

SYNOPSIS
     ps [-e] [-f] [-u USER] [-o LIST]

DESCRIPTION
     ps prints a line per process. With no options it prints the ones on
     this terminal: pid, terminal, processor time and command.

OPTIONS
     -e          every process, not only this terminal's
     -f          full: user, parent, start time and the whole command
     -u USER     only that user's
     -o LIST     choose the columns: pid, ppid, pgid, sid, user, uid,
                 tty, stat, time, etime, pri, nice, rss, vsz, comm, args

SEE ALSO
     top(1), pgrep(1), /proc in procfs
